   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here's a hopeful idea: everyone can change. Give a person a second chance and, with enough compassion, they'll take it."
    },
    {
     "text": "Often, that's true. But in chapter four of Suicidal Empathy, Gad Saad argues that we've turned a hope into a dogma."
    },
    {
     "text": "He calls it the blank slate felon: the belief that a criminal's past tells us nothing about his future."
    }
   ]
