   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here he borrows a term from zoology: kleptogamy, which biologists once nicknamed, rather crudely, the sneaky eff-er strategy."
    },
    {
     "text": "In some species, smaller males can't win fights with the big dominant male."
    },
    {
     "text": "In cuttlefish, for example, a small male can disguise himself with a female's markings,"
    },
    {
     "text": "slip past the big male, and mate on the sly."
    },
    {
     "text": "Saad's provocative claim is that some performative male allies are running a social version of the same strategy. It's a joke with a point, and plenty of people will find it unfair."
    }
   ]
