   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The hardest part of this chapter is about sexual violence."
    },
    {
     "text": "In 2016, in Freiburg, Germany, a nineteen-year-old medical student named Maria Ladenburger, who volunteered with refugees, was raped and murdered on her way home from a party."
    },
    {
     "text": "Her killer was an asylum seeker from Afghanistan who had earlier been convicted in Greece of attacking a woman and throwing her off a cliff, and had been released early. A German court sentenced him to life in prison."
    },
    {
     "text": "Her family asked mourners to give to refugee charities. Saad sees that as empathy that survives even this. Many others see it as grace."
    }
   ]
  },
