   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Saad lists court cases in Britain and Austria where men convicted of sexual crimes against children received sentences he calls shockingly light, sometimes with their cultural background raised in mitigation."
    },
    {
     "text": "And he cites Nadia Murad, a Yazidi woman enslaved and raped by ISIS, who won the Nobel Peace Prize. In 2021, a planned talk by her for Toronto students was called off, reportedly over worries it could stoke Islamophobia. After an outcry, the school board apologised."
