   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Critics raise strong points."
    },
    {
     "text": "Many people who leave prison never commit a violent crime, and well-run programs, like education and job training behind bars, do reduce reoffending."
    },
    {
     "text": "Individual horrors, however real, can't tell us about whole groups of migrants. Crime tracks age, sex, poverty and opportunity, as well as origin."
    },
    {
     "text": "And mercy and due process protect the innocent too. The system that sometimes frees a guilty man also saves the wrongly accused."
    },
    {
     "text": "Shared ground: victims deserve to come first, sentences should follow the evidence on who reoffends, and a second chance works best when it isn't the seventh."
    }
   ]
